{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>For honor and for splendor.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): that he be honored and glorified in them. And since the High Priest is the angel of YHWH of Hosts among individuals in the matter of the service, He now commands to clothe him in royal garments, and that he be a honored and glorified king among the multitude, and then he will be complete in all, for these garments are royal garments. The <i>me'il</i>, as it is written (II Samuel 13:18): ״כי כן תלבשנה בנות המלך הבתולות מעילים״; and the <i>ketonet tashbetz</i> is the <i>ketonet passim</i> spoken of regarding Joseph (Genesis 37:3): ״ויעש לו כתנת פסים״; and the <i>mitznefet</i> is the custom of the rulers and kings in the lands of Ishmael, that they wrap with it the neck and the head." "<b>And by way of</b> the Kabbalah: לכבוד ולתפארת — he says, ״ועשית בגדי קדש לאהרן אחיך,״ that he minister in them לכבוד ולתפארת, that is, for the honor of HaShem who dwells among them, and for the splendor of Israel. And you already know that the Mishkan was a model for the future Temple." "<b>And behold,</b> the Prophet called the Holy Temple בית קדשנו ותפארתנו. The intention is: the house of our Holy One — that is the honor; and of our splendor — that is the splendor of Israel. And this is (Amos 7:13): ״כי מקדש מלך ובית ממלכה הוא״. And this is what He said: לכהנו — with the addition of the letter ו״ו to allude to the sixth sefirah; and the word לי is like לה׳ — and that is the honor. And this is clear."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:05:02.682133743Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}